course: dictionary
lesson: 14898
title: Words that can be got back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Recoverable is made of two parts: «recover», which means to get something back, and «-able», which means can be done. So recoverable means able to be got back.
explain: «Mia deleted her homework by mistake, but the file is recoverable.» The clue is deleted: a deleted file has gone, so recoverable tells you Mia still has a chance to get it back.
explain: The word also works for people and illnesses. «The doctor said Sam's injury is fully recoverable.» The clues are doctor and injury. Swap in «can get better» and the sentence still makes sense, so recoverable means able to get better here.
fact: Recoverable means able to be got back, able to get better, or able to be paid back.
fact: «Recoverable» can describe lost or deleted files, photos and money.
fact: «Recoverable» can describe a person or an illness that can get better.
fact: «Recoverable» can also describe oil that can be taken out of the ground.
fact: The root word «recover» means to get something back or to get well again.
exercise: «Oscar's lost game save is recoverable.» What does recoverable mean here? | *Able to be got back | Gone for ever and never to be seen again | Very large and heavy | Painted bright green
exercise: «The bank said the lost money was recoverable.» What does recoverable suggest? | *The money can be claimed back | The money has been spent on sweets | The money is too shiny to count | The money is hidden under the bed
exercise: Which part of recoverable means to get something back? | file | able | *recover | deleted
test: «The storm damaged the roof, but the damage is recoverable.» What does recoverable mean? | Permanently broken with no hope | *Able to be put right and got back | Brand new and shiny | Too heavy to lift
test: Jayden says recoverable means exactly the same as lost. Is he right? | No, recoverable means very happy | *No, lost means gone, but recoverable means it can still be got back | Yes, both words describe bright colours | Yes, they mean exactly the same thing
exam: Which sentence uses recoverable to mean a person can get better? | *«The nurse said Tom's illness is recoverable, and he will be home soon.» | «Her old diary is recoverable from the bin.» | «The chair is recoverable and painted blue.» | «The river is recoverable and very wide.»
